Last completed
--------------
EviTrack search is now connected end-to-end to the existing internal guideline
retrieval infrastructure.

The frontend SearchBox sends a query to the EviTrack API. The backend creates
a BGE-small-en-v1.5 embedding and uses GuidelineRepository to retrieve the
five nearest guideline chunks from PostgreSQL/pgvector. The frontend renders
the returned evidence.

This is an internal guideline retrieval milestone only. External web
evidence discovery is the next major development stage.

Next
----
Implement the separate external evidence discovery layer.

The next stage should search public/external sources for evidence relevant to
a user query, such as prevalence, epidemiology, efficacy, safety, cost or
population data, and return source links for user review.

External evidence must remain separate from the existing guideline
grounding/retrieval mechanism.
